              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, is it true that the Commissioner of Social Security has paid EAJA awards directly to attorneys and continues to do so when the client has assigned the payment to an attorney?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3e7c092447d7bcc7749abe61fbb8a715dce0d53925efb7ca841f2d7f39213ca4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3e7c092447d7-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, what authority does a court have to direct that the money be paid to the attorney?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3e7c092447d7bcc7749abe61fbb8a715dce0d53925efb7ca841f2d7f39213ca4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3e7c092447d7-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, what would happen if the prevailing party were a prisoner; would the attorney fee be paid to the prisoner, and if not, to whom?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3e7c092447d7bcc7749abe61fbb8a715dce0d53925efb7ca841f2d7f39213ca4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3e7c092447d7-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, can trusts recover EAJA fees?"
      }
    ],
